{"type":"user","uuid":"01a0a9ad-4a07-7425-a127-8956d23796be","session_id":"01a0a9ac-dc77-7ede-9aa0-53ac9c6347ab","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_01a0a9ad170a73d38bede640","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"pnpm node-linker=hoisted setting official documentation\",\n  \"totalResults\": 17,\n  \"showing\": 10,\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"url\": \"pnpm.io/settings/node-modules\",\n      \"title\": \"Node-Modules & Hoisting Settings | pnpm\",\n      \"snippet\": \"`enableGlobalVirtualStore`\\n`virtualStoreType`\\n`PNPM_CONFIG_VIRTUAL_STORE_TYPE`\\n`pnpm config get virtualStoreType`\\n\\nThe setting is independent of `nodeLinker`: `isolated` and `pnp` both work with either store type, and `hoisted` writes no virtual store at all, so it is unaffected.\\n\\n`nodeLinker`\\n`isolated`\\n`pnp`\\n`hoisted`\\n\\n### enableGlobalVirtualStore\\n\\nAdded in: v10.12.1\\n\\nSince v11.23.0, `virtualStoreType` is the canonical spelling of this setting: `enableGlobalVirtualStore: true` is `virtualStor\",\n      \"source\": \"tavily\",\n      \"extra\": {\n        \"score\": 0.7763013,\n        \"trustLabel\": {\n          \"source\": \"retrieved\",\n          \"traceId\": \"30be9d0df79a4cc9bfb246eaa2e88757\"\n        },\n        \"trustDisposal\": \"stripped\",\n        \"trustSuspicious\": true\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"pnpm.io/settings\",\n      \"title\": \"Settings (pnpm-workspace.yaml)\",\n      \"snippet\": \"### Node-Modules Settings\\n\\nFull reference →\\n\\n modulesDir\\n nodeLinker\\n nodeExperimentalPackageMap\\n nodePackageMapType\\n symlink\\n enableModulesDir\\n virtualStoreDir\\n virtualStoreDirMaxLength\\n virtualStoreOnly\\n packageImportMethod\\n modulesCacheMaxAge\\n dlxCacheMaxAge\\n virtualStoreType\\n enableGlobalVirtualStore\\n\\n### Dependency Hoisting Settings\\n\\nFull reference →\\n\\n hoist\\n hoistWorkspacePackages\\n hoistPattern\\n publicHoistPattern\\n shamefullyHoist\\n hoistingLimits\\n\\n### Store Settings\\n\\nFull reference →\\n\\n \",\n      \"source\": \"tavily\",\n      \"extra\": {\n        \"score\": 0.7418428,\n        \"trustLabel\": {\n          \"source\": \"retrieved\",\n          \"traceId\": \"30be9d0df79a4cc9bfb246eaa2e88757\"\n        },\n        \"trustDisposal\": \"stripped\",\n        \"trustSuspicious\": true\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"pnpm.io/blog/2020/10/17/node-modules-configuration-options-with-pnpm\",\n      \"title\": \"Node-Modules configuration options with pnpm | pnpm\",\n      \"snippet\": \"hoist-pattern[]=\\n\\n; All types are hoisted to the root in order to make TypeScript happy\\n\\npublic-hoist-pattern[]=types\\n\\n; All ESLint-related packages are hoisted to the root as well\\n\\npublic-hoist-pattern[]=eslint`\\n\\n## Plug'n'Play. The strictest configuration\\n\\npnpm supports Yarn's Plug'n'Play since v5.9. With PnP, both your application and the dependencies of your application will have access only to their declared dependencies. This is even stricter then setting `hoist=false` because inside a mo\",\n      \"source\": \"tavily\",\n      \"extra\": {\n        \"score\": 0.7244226,\n        \"trustLabel\": {\n          \"source\": \"retrieved\",\n          \"traceId\": \"30be9d0df79a4cc9bfb246eaa2e88757\"\n        },\n        \"trustDisposal\": \"stripped\",\n        \"trustSuspicious\": true\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"pnpm.io/zh-TW/11.x/settings/node-modules\",\n      \"title\": \"Node-Modules & Hoisting Settings | pnpm\",\n      \"snippet\": \"```\\n\\n### shamefullyHoist\\n\\n 預設值：false\\n 型別：布林值\\n\\nBy default, pnpm creates a semistrict `node_modules`, meaning dependencies have access to undeclared dependencies but modules outside of `node_modules` do not. 使用此頁面配置，生態系統中的大多數套件將沒有問題的運作。 However, if some tooling only works when the hoisted dependencies are in the root of `node_modules`, you can set this to `true` to hoist them for you.\\n\\n### hoistingLimits\\n\\nAdded in: